// Repro for issues/typeid-diagnostic-suggests-a-nonexistent-is-builtin.md
//
// `typeid` takes a TYPE. Passing a VALUE produces a diagnostic that suggests
// an `is()` builtin, which the language does not have.
//
//   yo check issues/repros/typeid-on-a-value-suggests-is.yo
//
// expected (today):
//   error: typeid expects a type argument. Use is() or downcast() for runtime
//   type checks on Dyn values.
//
// NOTE the binding must be plain — wrapping it in `comptime_print(...)` hides
// the message behind "Failed to evaluate argument for comptime_print".
main :: (fn() -> unit)({
  x := i32(1);
  y := typeid(x);
  ()
});
export(main);
